  "turns": [
    {
      "input": "*He asks Sister Mereth who they think he is and where he comes from.*",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Sister Mereth studies him with the flat patience of someone accustomed to being asked strange questions by people with more confidence than sense. \"I don't know who you are,\" she says. \"You came to Saint Orra's House this morning asking after children, and now you're standing in Heartstone Square talking in circles. As for where you come from, you've given me nothing to think one place or another.\" She shifts the document bag on her shoulder, the leather strap creaking. \"If you've got a name and a straight purpose, I'd rather hear that than riddles about what I imagine. I've got a kitchen to see to and no time for guessing games.\"",
